      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "src/manta_trading_engine/core_model/value_checks.py:66-70"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Invalid timestamp meaning breaks the error contract",
      "description": "`Timestamp` does not validate its meaning field. Passing `Timestamp(100, \"available_at\")` into `SignalEvent` therefore raises `AttributeError` while formatting `.value`, rather than `InvalidSignalError`. Validate the enum before accessing `.value`, or format the rejected value with `repr`. Add tests for string and `None` meanings.",
